course: dictionary
lesson: 6550
title: A word for news
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A newsletter is a short sheet of news sent regularly to a group of people. It can be printed on paper or sent as an email. The word has a clue inside it: news and letter.
explain: «A lie told to one person can travel far, even into a club newsletter.» The clues are club and travel. A newsletter goes to a group, such as a club, and news spreads through it. So a newsletter is a kind of news sheet for many readers.
explain: «Wee Callum in Glasgow said he'd scored a hat-trick, and Dad was so chuffed (pleased) that the story reached the club newsletter.» The brackets tell you chuffed means pleased. The story was news, and the newsletter shared it with the club.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in "news sheet" for newsletter. If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right. A school newsletter tells parents about trips, events, holidays and achievements.
fact: A newsletter is a short printed sheet or email.
fact: It is sent regularly to a group of people.
fact: It gives news about a school, club, company or place.
fact: Useful phrases are «weekly newsletter» and «sign up for the newsletter».
fact: «Chuffed» means pleased, and «wee» (Scotland) means small.
exercise: «The school newsletter tells parents about trips, events and holidays.» What is a newsletter? | A type of school dinner | A long book with no pictures | A lock for the school gate | *A short sheet or email of news sent regularly to a group
exercise: «Dad was so chuffed that the story reached the club newsletter.» What does chuffed mean? | *Pleased | Angry and sulky | Tired after running | Lost
exercise: In «Wee Callum in Glasgow said he'd scored a hat-trick», which word means small? | scored | *wee | Glasgow | Callum
test: Ella's class is making a newsletter. Which of these would you find in one? | *Headlines and a short report about a school trip | A map of the moon | A recipe for toast | A bus timetable for next year
test: Which phrase means a newsletter that comes out every week? | A yearly diary | A nightly news | A quiet holiday | *A weekly newsletter
exam: «Sign up for the newsletter» most likely means | To write a letter by hand | To tear up the newsletter | *To join so you get the newsletter | To go to sleep early
